cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or data, please cite the accompanying manuscript."
title: "Do In-Match Hydration Breaks Alter Match Momentum? A Within-Match Case-Crossover Analysis of the 2026 FIFA World Cup"
authors:
  - family-names: Dey
    given-names: Debangan
    affiliation: "Department of Statistics, Texas A&M University"
    email: debangan@tamu.edu
year: 2026
version: "1.0.0"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  Reproducible code and derived data for a within-match case-crossover analysis
  of whether the 2026 FIFA World Cup mandatory hydration breaks affected match
  momentum, with an external-control robustness design and an event-based (xG)
  outcome check.
keywords:
  - hydration break
  - case-crossover design
  - match momentum
  - causal inference
  - association football
